// #188 (PERF-CLOSURE-NATIVE) reproducer, committed per R15.
//
// The third first-class closure call shape: a capturing closure RETURNED from a
// function and then called.
//
// Measured at e12c82d2 BEFORE the fix this shape produced
// `program_fallback: w17-marshal-residual` — the same module-binding
// misclassification the sibling file documents, which masked everything behind
// it. With that removed the real blocker is now visible and named:
//
//     program_fallback: jit-compile-error
//     Route A surface-and-stop: SURFACE — direct call to `mk` resolved to
//     function index N but has no compile-time-proven
//     FrameDescriptor.return_kind.
//
// A declared function-type return annotation (`(int) => int`) falls through
// `classify_type_annotation_metadata` in `shape-vm compiler/helpers.rs` to
// `FrameReturnMetadata::unknown()`, so the W36 named-function callgraph has no
// return-kind proof for `mk` and refuses the whole program. `ConcreteType::
// Function` already maps to `Ptr(HeapKind::Closure)` in
// `shape-value v2/capture_native_kind.rs`; the annotation arm is what is
// missing. Deliberately NOT fixed here — a function-typed slot has a documented
// dual carrier (`Arc<HeapValue::ClosureRaw>` vs a NaN-boxed `box_function`
// ref), so stamping a return kind is a soundness-sensitive change that needs
// its own slice and its own differential.
//
// The value of this file meanwhile is the VM==JIT anchor: whichever tier runs
// it, the output must be identical, and the bail must stay a bail rather than
// becoming silent wrong output.

fn mk(k: int) -> (int) => int { return |x: int| x * k }

let f = mk(3)
let mut total = 0
for i in 0..200 {
    total = total + f(i)
}
print(total)
